  <title>Time clock</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>General</gui><gui>Time clock</gui></guiseq>, or the
  <gui>Time Clock</gui> button of the main window, lists the employees, with
  the time and project of anyone punched in. Leave it open where employees can
  reach it.</p>

  <section id="in">
  <title>Punching in</title>
  <steps>
    <item><p>Double click your name, or scan or type your employee id into
    the box above the list and press <key>Enter</key>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Double click the job or project you are working on, or scan or
    type its id. The list holds the <link xref="job_sheet">job sheets</link>
    and <link xref="manufacturing">manufacturing projects</link> made
    available in the time clock, and the permanent projects from <link
    xref="settings#time_clock">the settings</link>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Punch in</gui>, or press <key>I</key>.</p></item>
  </steps>
  </section>

  <section id="out">
  <title>Punching out</title>
  <p>Double click your name, or scan your id, and click <gui>Punch out</gui>,
  or press <key>O</key>. <gui>Cancel</gui>, or <key>C</key>, goes back to the
  list without punching.</p>
  <p>Double click the <gui>Time</gui> of someone punched in to see how long
  they have been in.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="manual">
  <title>Forgot to punch?</title>
  <p>Under <gui>Manual punchin</gui> or <gui>Manual punchout</gui>, use the
  arrow buttons to move the day, hour and minute to when you really came in or
  left, then click its <gui>Punch in</gui> or <gui>Punch out</gui>. To help
  you remember, the window shows how long ago you last punched in and out on
  that job, and how many times you have punched in on it.</p>
  </section>

  <p>Hours punched on a customer's job sheet can be billed with <link
  xref="invoice#time_clock">Import time clock</link> on their invoice.
  Corrections to punches already made are done in <link
  xref="time_clock_tool"/>.</p>

</page>
